Third-party components and attribution

The MIT license above applies to the original work in this project. The
following components carry their own terms and remain subject to them:

1. GFN-FF force field implementation (`src/gfnff/`) — a faithful Rust port
   of the GFN-FF implementation in xtb (https://github.com/grimme-lab/xtb),
   distributed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0 or later.
   Copyright the xtb developers. Method: Spicher & Grimme,
   Angew. Chem. Int. Ed. 2020, 59, 15665.

2. RDKit WebAssembly build (`app/vendor/RDKit_minimal.js`,
   `RDKit_minimal.wasm`) — Copyright the RDKit contributors.
   BSD-3-Clause; see `app/vendor/RDKit-LICENSE.txt`.

3. 3Dmol.js (`app/vendor/3Dmol-min.js`) — Copyright the 3Dmol.js
   contributors. BSD-3-Clause; see `app/vendor/3Dmol-LICENSE.txt`.

4. JSME molecule editor (`app/vendor/jsme/`) — Copyright 2017 Novartis
   Institutes for BioMedical Research Inc and Bruno Bienfait.
   BSD-3-Clause; see `app/vendor/jsme/license.txt`.

5. Ketcher chemical structure editor + Indigo toolkit, prebuilt bundle
   (`app/vendor/ketcher/`, ketcher-react 3.18.0 + ketcher-standalone
   3.18.0 + Indigo 1.46.0 wasm, bundled once with esbuild) — Copyright
   (c) EPAM Systems, Inc. Apache-2.0; see `app/vendor/ketcher/LICENSE`.

6. MMFF94/MMFF94s parameter data (extracted under `src/mmff/`) and LBDD
   reference data (`app/lbdd_data.js`: PAINS/BRENK SMARTS catalogs, QED
   constants) — extracted from the RDKit source tree (BSD-3-Clause);
   MMFF94 parameters derive from the published work of T. A. Halgren.
